PULSAR-CPU
==========

PULSAR-CPU is implemented as an extension to OpenFHE 1.4.0.

Files originating from OpenFHE retain their original BSD 2-Clause notices.
The Z-domain and Boolean-to-Boolean bootstrapping implementation is adapted
from the FHE-SIMD-ALU OpenFHE prototype. PULSAR-CPU bundles the required
source files so that FHE-SIMD-ALU is not a separate build or runtime
dependency. This provenance statement does not imply that the PULSAR
operators or scheduler are part of OpenFHE or FHE-SIMD-ALU.

PULSAR-specific components include the dense Boolean representation, complex
parallel-prefix operators, Prefix Boot integration, circuit-oriented refresh
scheduler, multiplication path, and application benchmarks.

The offline build bundle also contains pinned source releases of Intel HEXL,
Google cpu_features, cereal, and gperftools. Their upstream license and
attribution files are retained in the corresponding source archives under
vendor/.
